{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"ignitable-noteworthy-osprey","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Discovered while landing e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a (Gerrit change 2436). CI's\nbuild-and-test / pytest job failed 3 consecutive times (all 3 python\nversions each time) on the exact same test:\n\ntests/unit/test_audit_serve_heldout.py::test_serve_binds_loopback_ephemeral_and_lists_ticket\n\nFailure: RuntimeError: Network access is forbidden in unit/scripts tests...\nraised despite the test carrying @pytest.mark.allow_network, which should\nmake tests/conftest.py's autouse _network_guard fixture skip patching\nsocket.socket.connect for this test.\n\nRoot-cause evidence gathered (not yet fully diagnosed):\n- The test passes 100% reliably when run in isolation, or in small subsets,\n  including with -n 4 --dist worksteal (5+ repeated local runs, 0 failures).\n- The test only fails as part of a FULL-suite parallel run (pytest -m \"not\n  integration and not external and not repo_policy\" -n 4 --dist worksteal\n  against the whole tests/ tree) -- reproduced identically on 2 separate\n  local full-suite runs, which is consistent with the CI failure signature.\n- The same full-suite run also non-deterministically fails several OTHER,\n  unrelated tests under load (test_atomic_completion_close.py,\n  test_rebar_repo_isolation.py, test_tracker_footprint_cli.py) -- none of\n  which share any code path with the audit-serve test or with e9d5's\n  change, suggesting a general resource-contention/timing sensitivity\n  across several tests when the full suite runs under xdist worksteal,\n  not a defect specific to any one test or diff.\n- This test spins up a REAL uvicorn server on a background thread and\n  polls for readiness with a 10s deadline, then makes a REAL HTTP request\n  to it -- exactly the kind of test that is sensitive to CPU/scheduler\n  contention under a busy parallel test run.\n\nNot fixed as part of e9d5 -- unrelated to that ticket's scope (typed\nreconciler payload contracts), and per this repo's flaky-test policy a\nflake must be root-caused rather than silently retried; this ticket is\nthe tracking vehicle for that root-cause.\n\nSuggested follow-up:\n- Confirm whether this and/or the other tests observed failing under load\n  are known-flaky (check CI history across other recent changes for the\n  same signature).\n- If confirmed timing-sensitive under contention, consider widening the\n  10s startup deadline model, isolating this test from -n xdist parallel\n  scheduling (xdist_group), or another fix appropriate to its actual root\n  cause once diagnosed.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Root cause identified for why test_serve_binds_loopback_ephemeral_and_lists_ticket\n  (and, if related, the other full-suite-only failures named above) fail\n  under parallel/full-suite load but never in isolation.\n- A fix applied (or a documented decision not to fix, e.g. an accepted\n  ADR on test parallelism tradeoffs) and the affected test(s) demonstrated\n  stable across N repeated full-suite CI runs.","id":"edeb-c3ad-c051-4e6a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky test_serve_binds_loopback_ephemeral_and_lists_ticket under full-suite parallel load"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788116857920221001,"uuid":"72e45524-8142-42aa-bf7c-fd334f5a94a8"}